Package: rhodep-flashlight
Version: 1
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: rhodep port
Depends: gpiod
Description: Camera-flash torch enable for Motorola rhodep
 The rear flash is an analog current-driver IC that needs its enable on
 tlmm 49 held asserted for as long as it is lit -- a one-shot level write is
 not enough (the LED dies a second later when the gpio request is released).
 This service holds tlmm 49 low for the session. The light itself is the
 pwm-leds "white:torch" node (PWM current source on PM6125 GPIO8), which KDE
 Plasma's flashlight button toggles. With the enable held, the button turns
 the torch cleanly on and off.
